summary: SIGPIPE is ignored once the hosted entry has established the POSIX layer, so a write to a pipe whose reading end is closed is epipe and the program goes on, while posix.spawn gives a child SIGPIPE's default back, so a shell writing into a pipe the parent has closed is signalled with 13 rather than exiting after a failed write
